From 013127e890c74ab56402989dd0b090bd336d9cd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:09:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/46] feat(crypto): compressed encrypted chunks (ENCR_COMPR),
 both ways

proxmox-backup-client compresses then encrypts chunks and blobs by
default: DataBlob::encode(compress = true) runs zstd::bulk::compress, a
regular zstd frame, before AES-256-GCM, with ENCR_COMPR_BLOB_MAGIC_1_0.
Such blobs were rejected on read ("zstd block format not supported"), so
encrypted backups made with the official client could not be restored,
and our encrypted chunks were uploaded uncompressed.

- DecodeEncryptedBlob decrypts ENCR_COMPR and zstd-decodes the frame,
  then checks the digest on the plaintext.
- EncodeEncryptedCompressed compresses with the configured level and
  keeps the compressed form only when smaller, as PBS does; UploadChunk
  uses it for compressed uploads, and encrypted blobs are compressed.
- Golden vector built with libzstd + OpenSSL the way PBS builds it
  (testdata/gen_encr_compr_vector.py).
